{"review_id": "REV-10", "question_id": "c554a453b6b99d8b59e4ef1511b1b506ff6e5aa4", "paper_arxiv_id": "1905.10044", "manifest_item_index": 226, "actual_model": "llama3.2:1b", "blind_label_in_signed_sheet": "Model_Alpha", "model_by_original_mapping": "llama3.2:3b", "attribution_changed": true, "match_method": "exact", "final_primary_label": "SUPPORTED", "final_secondary_label": "", "is_adjudicated_change": "NO", "original_primary_label": "SUPPORTED", "is_refusal": false, "token_f1": 0.5339, "automated_containment_proxy": 0.7333, "latency_s": 10.4451, "tokens_per_second": 19.56, "answer": "The dataset was built by collecting questions from anonymized, aggregated queries to the Google search engine. These queries were then heuristically identified as likely to be yes/no questions, and the first word of each question was used to construct a set of indicator words. The questions were then kept if a Wikipedia page was returned as one of the first five results, and annotators labeled question/article pairs in a three-step process, including deciding if the question was good, finding a passage within the document that contained enough information to answer the question, and marking the question's answer as \"yes\" or \"no\"."}
