{"review_id": "REV-16", "question_id": "81dc39ee6cdacf90d5f0f62134bf390a29146c65", "paper_arxiv_id": "1911.03310", "manifest_item_index": 376, "actual_model": "qwen2.5:0.5b", "blind_label_in_signed_sheet": "Model_Beta", "model_by_original_mapping": "llama3.2:3b", "attribution_changed": true, "match_method": "exact", "final_primary_label": "UNSUPPORTED", "final_secondary_label": "", "is_adjudicated_change": "NO", "original_primary_label": "UNSUPPORTED", "is_refusal": false, "token_f1": 0.2069, "automated_containment_proxy": 0.3021, "latency_s": 5.4236, "tokens_per_second": 56.14, "answer": "This work presents several challenges that must be addressed to build better language-neutral representations. Firstly, the context provided suggests that the current approach of using mBERT contextual embeddings does not directly translate well into zero-shot cross-lingual tasks. This implies that the embeddings may not be as effective in representing similar semantic phenomena across different languages. Secondly, the work highlights the need for a more comprehensive understanding of the semantic phenomena that mBERT contextual embeddings are designed to represent. This requires a deeper analysis of the specific tasks and applications for which these embeddings are being used. Lastly, the challenge of ensuring that the embeddings are not only contextually relevant but also contextually neutral is also addressed. This means that the embeddings should not only capture the semantic relationships between words but also the contextual relationships between words and sentences."}
